# Titan CredentialKeyProvider SPI — discovered by java.util.ServiceLoader.
#
# Order matters: providers are tried in the chain top-to-bottom, first non-null KEK wins.
# See io.adaptiq.titan.flow.crypto.CredentialKeyProvider#active() for the chain semantics.
#
# 1. EnvKeyProvider — reads TITAN_KEK (the env var the rig/helm chart sets). Closes #874:
#    previously nothing read TITAN_KEK and deployments had to fall back to DevAuto.
# 2. DevAutoKeyProvider — dev-only, inert unless TITAN_CREDENTIALS_DEV_AUTO_KEK=true.
#    When the flag is unset (the default) it returns null and the chain falls through to
#    the env / Infisical / KMS providers. This is the load-bearing safety property —
#    production deployments still fail closed without an explicit KEK. See #800.
io.adaptiq.titan.credentials.EnvKeyProvider
io.adaptiq.titan.credentials.DevAutoKeyProvider
